<script data-page="app" type="application/json">{"component":"flashcards\/study","props":{"errors":{},"name":"Topwords","auth":{"user":{"id":5,"name":"\u00c1rp\u00e1d Szaniszl\u00f3","email":"developedbybarley@gmail.com","email_verified_at":null,"two_factor_confirmed_at":null,"streak":17,"quiz_completions":1,"text_analyses":14,"last_activity_date":"2026-05-20T00:00:00.000000Z","onboarding_completed_at":"2026-04-18T19:40:25.000000Z","created_at":"2026-04-18T19:40:03.000000Z","updated_at":"2026-05-20T08:29:24.000000Z","stripe_id":"cus_UR8u0ziMkWwJIo","pm_type":null,"pm_last_four":null,"trial_ends_at":null,"ai_access":false,"subscriptions":[]},"isAdmin":true,"subscription":{"hasActiveAccess":true,"isSubscribed":false,"isPremium":false,"hasAiAccess":false,"isOnTrial":false}},"sidebarOpen":true,"flash":{"streakTriggered":null,"success":null,"achievements":[],"calibrationPrompt":null,"showTour":false,"importedCardId":null},"deck":{"id":38,"name":"May"},"cards":[{"id":51304,"front":"<p>I didn&#039;t mean to _______ you with my comment; I was just trying to be honest. <em>(megs\u00e9rteni \/ megb\u00e1ntani)<\/em><\/p><p>The politician&#039;s controversial remarks are likely to _______ a significant portion of the electorate. <em>(felh\u00e1bor\u00edtani \/ s\u00e9rteni)<\/em><\/p><p>Some people find it easy to _______ others without even realizing it, due to cultural differences. <em>(megb\u00e1ntani \/ s\u00e9rt\u00e9st okozni)<\/em><\/p><p>His refusal to apologize seemed to _______ her more than the initial insult itself. <em>(felingerelni \/ bosszantani)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">megs\u00e9rteni \/ megb\u00e1ntani \/ felh\u00e1bor\u00edtani<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): megnyugtatni \/ \u00f6r\u00f6met szerezni \/ kedv\u00e9ben j\u00e1rni<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ someone = megs\u00e9rteni valakit (pl. I didn&#039;t want to _______ anyone with my opinion.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ deeply = m\u00e9lyen megb\u00e1ntani (pl. Her words seemed to _______ him deeply.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ easily = k\u00f6nnyen megs\u00e9rt\u0151dni (pl. He tends to _______ easily, so be careful what you say.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ public sensibilities = s\u00e9rteni a k\u00f6z\u00edzl\u00e9st (pl. The advertisement was criticized for seeming to _______ public sensibilities.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>offend<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>offensive<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>offensively<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>offense<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>offend<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: easily offend \/ offend someone \/ offend deeply \/ offend by<\/span><\/p><p>similar: insult \/ displease \/ annoy \/ upset<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: please \/ delight \/ flatter<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-21T16:21:17+00:00"},{"id":51315,"front":"<p>We had to call a plumber because the _______ in our bathroom was leaking badly. <em>(v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-rendszer \/ cs\u0151h\u00e1l\u00f3zat)<\/em><\/p><p>Modern building codes require specific standards for the installation of new _______. <em>(v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-szerel\u00e9s \/ v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-rendszer ki\u00e9p\u00edt\u00e9se)<\/em><\/p><p>The city&#039;s aging _______ infrastructure is a major concern for public health officials. <em>(v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-h\u00e1l\u00f3zat \/ cs\u0151rendszer)<\/em><\/p><p>He learned the basics of _______ by helping his father with repairs around the house. <em>(v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-szerel\u00e9s \/ v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-szerel\u0151i munka)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-szerel\u00e9s \/ v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-rendszer \/ cs\u0151h\u00e1l\u00f3zat<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): sz\u00e1razs\u00e1g \/ v\u00edzhi\u00e1ny \/ v\u00edztelens\u00e9g<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 leaky _______ = sziv\u00e1rg\u00f3 v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k (pl. We need to fix the leaky _______ before it causes more damage.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 indoor _______ = belt\u00e9ri v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-rendszer (pl. The house was old and lacked modern indoor _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 emergency _______ = s\u00fcrg\u0151ss\u00e9gi v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-szerel\u00e9s (pl. He offers 24-hour emergency _______ services.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 do the _______ = elv\u00e9gezni a v\u00edzvezet\u00e9k-szerel\u00e9st (pl. They hired a professional to do the _______ for their new kitchen.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>plumbing<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>plumbing<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: plumbing system \/ plumbing problems \/ plumbing fixtures \/ plumbing work<\/span><\/p><p>similar: pipework \/ piping \/ drainage system \/ water system<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: dryness \/ dehydration \/ aridity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"plumbing","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-21T23:32:46+00:00"},{"id":51305,"front":"<p>He suffered a severe _______ that left him partially paralyzed on one side. <em>(sz\u00e9l\u00fct\u00e9s \/ agyi \u00e9rkatasztr\u00f3fa)<\/em><\/p><p>With a gentle _______ of the cat&#039;s fur, she calmed it down. <em>(simogat\u00e1s \/ \u00e9rint\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>The artist&#039;s bold brush _______ defined the dramatic landscape. <em>(ecsetvon\u00e1s \/ von\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>The clock began to _______ midnight, signaling the new year. <em>(\u00fctni \/ kongatni)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">sz\u00e9l\u00fct\u00e9s \/ simogat\u00e1s \/ \u00fct\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): eg\u00e9szs\u00e9g \/ nyugalom \/ mozdulatlans\u00e1g<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 have a _______ = sz\u00e9l\u00fct\u00e9st kap (pl. He had a mild _______ last year.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 suffer a _______ = sz\u00e9l\u00fct\u00e9st szenved (pl. She suffered a major _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ of luck = szerencsevon\u00e1s (pl. It was a _______ of luck that we found it.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ of genius = zseni\u00e1lis h\u00faz\u00e1s (pl. That decision was a _______ of genius.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 heat _______ = h\u0151guta (pl. Be careful not to get heat _______ in this weather.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>stroke<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>stroke<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>stroke<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: brain stroke \/ gentle stroke \/ brush stroke \/ stroke of luck<\/span><\/p><p>similar: apoplexy \/ caress \/ pat \/ blow<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: health \/ calm \/ stillness<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-22T11:32:16+00:00"},{"id":51294,"front":"<p>I have no idea _______ what happened to the keys. <em>(egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n \/ semmif\u00e9le)<\/em><\/p><p>There was no evidence _______ to suggest he was involved. <em>(egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n \/ semmi)<\/em><\/p><p>She received no support _______ from her family during the difficult time. <em>(semmilyen \/ egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n)<\/em><\/p><p>The new policy had no impact _______ on the company&#039;s profits. <em>(egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n \/ semmi)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n \/ semmilyen \/ semmi<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): valamennyi \/ b\u00e1rmilyen \/ sok<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 nothing _______ = egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n semmi (pl. There was nothing _______ left.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 no one _______ = egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n senki (pl. No one _______ believed him.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 none _______ = egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n egy sem (pl. None _______ of them showed up.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 no reason _______ = egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n semmi ok (pl. There&#039;s no reason _______ to worry.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>whatsoever<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>whatsoever<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: nothing whatsoever \/ no one whatsoever \/ none whatsoever \/ no reason whatsoever<\/span><\/p><p>similar: at all \/ in any way \/ of any kind \/ in the slightest<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: any \/ some \/ a lot<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-18T19:43:06+00:00"},{"id":51297,"front":"<p>After hours of cooking, the vegetables turned into a soft, unappetizing _______. <em>(p\u00e9pes massza \/ k\u00e1sa)<\/em><\/p><p>His sentimental speech was full of emotional _______, rather than concrete arguments. <em>(\u00e9rzelg\u0151ss\u00e9g \/ ny\u00e1ladz\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>The prolonged rain turned the hiking trail into a muddy _______, making progress difficult. <em>(s\u00e1r \/ dagony\u00e1s talaj)<\/em><\/p><p>Don't _______ the potatoes too much; we want them creamy, not a watery paste. <em>(p\u00e9pes\u00edt \/ sz\u00e9tnyom)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 197, 94);\">p\u00e9pes\u00edt \/ p\u00e9pes massza \/ \u00e9rzelg\u0151ss\u00e9g \/ p\u00e9pes<\/span><\/p><p><span>Negative meaning (HU): szil\u00e1rd \/ kem\u00e9ny \/ t\u00f6m\u00f6r<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 turn to _______ = p\u00e9pes massz\u00e1v\u00e1 v\u00e1lik (pl. The overcooked apples turned to _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 emotional _______ = \u00e9rzelg\u0151ss\u00e9g (pl. Her letter was full of emotional _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a muddy _______ = s\u00e1ros massza\/dagony\u00e1s talaj (pl. The field was a muddy _______ after the storm.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ up = p\u00e9pesre nyom (pl. You need to _______ up the bananas for the baby.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>mush<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>mushy<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>mush<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>mush<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: baby mush \/ apple mush \/ emotional mush \/ turn to mush<\/span><\/p><p>similar: pulp \/ paste \/ slop \/ sentimentality<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: solidity \/ firmness \/ clarity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":1,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-21T18:07:41+00:00"},{"id":51287,"front":"<p>Please _______ of your waste responsibly by using the recycling bins provided. <em>(megszabadul \/ eldob \/ kidob)<\/em><\/p><p>The company decided to _______ of its non-essential assets to reduce debt. <em>(elad \/ \u00e9rt\u00e9kes\u00edt \/ megszabadul)<\/em><\/p><p>He was able to _______ of the problem quickly and efficiently. <em>(megold \/ elint\u00e9z \/ rendez)<\/em><\/p><p>The general will _______ his troops for battle at dawn. <em>(elrendez \/ fel\u00e1ll\u00edt \/ csatarendbe \u00e1ll\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">megszabadul \/ elrendez \/ elad<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): megtart \/ meg\u0151riz \/ beszerez<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ of something = megszabadul valamit\u0151l (pl. We need to dispose of these old documents.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ of waste = hullad\u00e9kot elhelyez\/kidob (pl. How do you dispose of hazardous waste?)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ of assets = vagyont\u00e1rgyakat elad\/megszabadul t\u0151l\u00fck (pl. The firm plans to dispose of its foreign assets.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ of a problem = megold egy probl\u00e9m\u00e1t (pl. He quickly disposed of the minor issue.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>dispose<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>disposable<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>disposal<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>dispose<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: dispose of \/ waste dispose \/ assets dispose \/ properly dispose<\/span><\/p><p>similar: discard \/ get rid of \/ sell \/ arrange<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: keep \/ retain \/ acquire<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T16:20:50+00:00"},{"id":51279,"front":"<p>The police asked the suspect to _______ his weapon. <em>(fegyvertelen\u00edt \/ leadja a fegyver\u00e9t)<\/em><\/p><p>The treaty aimed to _______ the region and prevent further conflict. <em>(lefenntartja a b\u00e9k\u00e9t \/ cs\u00f6kkenti a fegyverkez\u00e9st)<\/em><\/p><p>The diplomat&#039;s skillful negotiation helped to _______ the tense situation between the two nations. <em>(enyh\u00edt \/ csillap\u00edt \/ b\u00e9k\u00edttet)<\/em><\/p><p>He tried to _______ her fears by explaining the safety measures in place. <em>(csillap\u00edt \/ enyh\u00edt \/ megnyugtat)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">fegyvertelen\u00edt \/ lefegyverez \/ csillap\u00edt \/ enyh\u00edt \/ b\u00e9k\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): felfegyverez \/ fegyverkezik \/ fegyvereket szerez<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a weapon = lefegyverez egy fegyvert (pl. The officer ordered the robber to disarm a weapon.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ the enemy = lefegyverezni az ellens\u00e9get (pl. null)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ the region = lefegyverezni a r\u00e9gi\u00f3t (pl. The international community is working to disarm the region.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ fears = csillap\u00edtani a f\u00e9lelmeket (pl. null)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>disarm<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>disarmament<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>disarm<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: disarm a weapon \/ disarm the enemy \/ disarm the region \/ disarm fears<\/span><\/p><p>similar: demilitarize \/ de-escalate \/ pacify \/ appease<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: arm \/ equip \/ weaponize<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"disarm\ndisarmament","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":4,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"5 nap","good":"8 nap","easy":"10 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-28T16:21:33+00:00"},{"id":51320,"front":"<p>After years of practice, she became incredibly _______ in playing the piano, effortlessly performing complex pieces. <em>(\u00fcgyes \/ j\u00e1rtas)<\/em><\/p><p>To be truly _______ in a foreign language, one must not only understand grammar but also grasp cultural nuances. <em>(foly\u00e9kony \/ magabiztos)<\/em><\/p><p>The new software engineer is highly _______ in Python and C++, making him a valuable asset to the development team. <em>(szak\u00e9rt\u0151 \/ kompetens)<\/em><\/p><p>Her _______ command of legal terminology impressed the judges during the trial. <em>(mesteri \/ kiv\u00e1l\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">j\u00e1rtas \/ \u00fcgyes \/ szak\u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00fcgyetlen \/ tudatlan \/ hozz\u00e1 nem \u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in something = j\u00e1rtas valamiben (pl. He is proficient in several programming languages.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 highly _______ = nagyon j\u00e1rtas (pl. She is highly proficient at public speaking.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 become _______ = j\u00e1rtass\u00e1 v\u00e1lik (pl. With practice, you will become proficient.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ user = j\u00e1rtas felhaszn\u00e1l\u00f3 (pl. The software is designed for proficient users.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>proficiently<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>proficiency<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: proficient in \/ highly proficient \/ become proficient \/ proficient user<\/span><\/p><p>similar: skilled \/ competent \/ expert \/ adept<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: unskilled \/ incompetent \/ inexperienced<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"proficient\nproficiently\nproficiency","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T16:30:55+00:00"},{"id":51323,"front":"<p>After years of touring, the popular rock band decided to _______ and pursue solo careers. <em>(feloszlatja mag\u00e1t \/ sz\u00e9toszlik)<\/em><\/p><p>The government announced its intention to _______ the special task force once its mission was complete. <em>(feloszlat \/ megsz\u00fcntet)<\/em><\/p><p>Due to lack of funding, the research group had no choice but to _______ its operations. <em>(felsz\u00e1mol \/ besz\u00fcntet)<\/em><\/p><p>The general ordered his troops to _______ and return to their respective garrisons. <em>(sz\u00e9tsz\u00e9led \/ feloszlik)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">feloszlat \/ sz\u00e9toszlat \/ felsz\u00e1mol<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00f6sszegy\u0171jt \/ alak\u00edt \/ szervez<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a band = feloszlatni egy zenekart (pl. They decided to _______ a band after their last album.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an army = feloszlatni egy hadsereget (pl. The treaty required them to _______ an army.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a committee = feloszlatni egy bizotts\u00e1got (pl. The chairman chose to _______ a committee.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a group = feloszlatni egy csoportot (pl. The leader had to _______ a group due to internal conflicts.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>disband<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>disbandment<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>disband<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: disband a group \/ disband an organization \/ disband a committee \/ disband a military unit<\/span><\/p><p>similar: dissolve \/ break up \/ demobilize \/ scatter<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: assemble \/ form \/ create<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"disband","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T16:20:07+00:00"},{"id":51327,"front":"<p>I sent her a text message, but she didn&#039;t _______. <em>(v\u00e1laszol \/ felel)<\/em><\/p><p>The government has promised to _______ to public concerns about the new policy. <em>(reag\u00e1l \/ int\u00e9zkedik)<\/em><\/p><p>In an emergency, it&#039;s crucial to _______ quickly and effectively. <em>(cselekszik \/ reag\u00e1l)<\/em><\/p><p>The survey aims to understand how consumers _______ to different advertising strategies. <em>(viszonyul \/ reag\u00e1l)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">v\u00e1laszol \/ reag\u00e1l \/ felel<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): nem v\u00e1laszol \/ ignor\u00e1l \/ figyelmen k\u00edv\u00fcl hagy<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ to a question = v\u00e1laszol egy k\u00e9rd\u00e9sre (pl. He refused to _______ to a direct question.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ to a stimulus = reag\u00e1l egy ingerre (pl. The plant will _______ to light by growing towards it.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ to treatment = reag\u00e1l a kezel\u00e9sre (pl. The patient is _______ well to the new treatment.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ to an email = v\u00e1laszol egy e-mailre (pl. Please _______ to my email by tomorrow.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>respond<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>responsive<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>responsively<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>response<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>respond<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: respond to \/ respond quickly \/ respond effectively \/ respond positively<\/span><\/p><p>similar: reply \/ answer \/ react \/ retort<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: ignore \/ disregard \/ overlook<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"respond","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T10:15:09+00:00"},{"id":51323,"front":"<p>After years of touring, the popular rock band decided to _______ and pursue solo careers. <em>(feloszlatja mag\u00e1t \/ sz\u00e9toszlik)<\/em><\/p><p>The government announced its intention to _______ the special task force once its mission was complete. <em>(feloszlat \/ megsz\u00fcntet)<\/em><\/p><p>Due to lack of funding, the research group had no choice but to _______ its operations. <em>(felsz\u00e1mol \/ besz\u00fcntet)<\/em><\/p><p>The general ordered his troops to _______ and return to their respective garrisons. <em>(sz\u00e9tsz\u00e9led \/ feloszlik)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">feloszlat \/ sz\u00e9toszlat \/ felsz\u00e1mol<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00f6sszegy\u0171jt \/ alak\u00edt \/ szervez<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a band = feloszlatni egy zenekart (pl. They decided to _______ a band after their last album.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an army = feloszlatni egy hadsereget (pl. The treaty required them to _______ an army.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a committee = feloszlatni egy bizotts\u00e1got (pl. The chairman chose to _______ a committee.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a group = feloszlatni egy csoportot (pl. The leader had to _______ a group due to internal conflicts.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>disband<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>disbandment<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>disband<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: disband a group \/ disband an organization \/ disband a committee \/ disband a military unit<\/span><\/p><p>similar: dissolve \/ break up \/ demobilize \/ scatter<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: assemble \/ form \/ create<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"disband","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T16:34:33+00:00"},{"id":51289,"front":"<p>I _______ your call; please let me know when you&#039;re free to chat. <em>(v\u00e1rom \/ v\u00e1rakozom)<\/em><\/p><p>The committee&#039;s decision on the new policy is eagerly _______ by all stakeholders. <em>(v\u00e1rja \/ el\u0151re l\u00e1tja)<\/em><\/p><p>A significant challenge _______ the research team as they delve deeper into the complex data. <em>(v\u00e1r \/ el\u0151tt\u00fck \u00e1ll)<\/em><\/p><p>In the quiet of the morning, she sat by the window, _______ the first rays of dawn. <em>(v\u00e1rva \/ lesve)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">v\u00e1r \/ v\u00e1rakozik \/ el\u0151tt \u00e1ll<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elker\u00fcl \/ kiker\u00fcl \/ megsz\u00f6kik<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 eagerly _______ = t\u00fcrelmetlen\u00fcl v\u00e1r (pl. We eagerly _______ the results of the competition.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ your arrival = v\u00e1rja az \u00e9rkez\u00e9s\u00e9t (pl. They will _______ your arrival at the airport.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a decision = d\u00f6nt\u00e9sre v\u00e1r (pl. The whole country is awaiting a decision from the government.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a response = v\u00e1laszra v\u00e1r (pl. I am still _______ a response to my email.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>await<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>await<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: eagerly await \/ await your arrival \/ await a decision \/ await a response<\/span><\/p><p>similar: wait for \/ expect \/ anticipate \/ look forward to<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: avoid \/ dodge \/ evade<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":4,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"5 nap","good":"8 nap","easy":"10 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-24T16:18:22+00:00"},{"id":51307,"front":"<p>Could you show me the _______ to the nearest post office? <em>(\u00fat \/ ir\u00e1ny)<\/em><\/p><p>The new policy offers a more efficient _______ of achieving our sustainability goals. <em>(m\u00f3d \/ elj\u00e1r\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>In a _______, the project was a resounding success, exceeding all expectations. <em>(\u00f6sszess\u00e9g\u00e9ben \/ \u00e1ltal\u00e1noss\u00e1gban)<\/em><\/p><p>She has a unique _______ of looking at problems, which often leads to innovative solutions. <em>(szeml\u00e9letm\u00f3d \/ l\u00e1t\u00e1sm\u00f3d)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">\u00fat \/ m\u00f3d \/ ir\u00e1ny<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): akad\u00e1ly \/ zs\u00e1kutca \/ t\u00e9ved\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 by the _______ = mellesleg, aprop\u00f3 (pl. By the _______, have you seen John today?)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 in a big _______ = nagym\u00e9rt\u00e9kben, nagyon (pl. He helped me in a big _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 make _______ = halad, el\u0151rejut (pl. We&#039;re making good _______ with the renovations.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 lose your _______ = elveszti a fej\u00e9t, d\u00fchbe gurul (pl. Don&#039;t lose your _______ over such a small mistake.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 on the _______ = \u00faton, \u00fatk\u00f6zben (pl. I&#039;m on the _______ to the office now.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>way<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>way<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: the right way \/ no way \/ this way \/ by the way<\/span><\/p><p>similar: path \/ route \/ method \/ manner<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: obstacle \/ barrier \/ dead end<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-22T16:21:13+00:00"},{"id":51268,"front":"<p>He&#039;s so _______, he never changes his mind even when he&#039;s wrong. <em>(makacs \/ merev)<\/em><\/p><p>Despite the overwhelming evidence, the committee remained _______ in its decision. <em>(hajthatatlan \/ kitart\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p>The research highlights the _______ nature of certain societal attitudes, resisting reform. <em>(kem\u00e9ny \/ rugalmatlan)<\/em><\/p><p>Her _______ refusal to compromise threatened to derail the entire negotiation. <em>(szil\u00e1rd \/ engedetlen)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">makacs \/ kem\u00e9ny \/ merev \/ hajthatatlan \/ szil\u00e1rd<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): enged\u00e9keny \/ rugalmas \/ nyitott<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ child = makacs gyerek (pl. My _______ child refuses to eat vegetables.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ to = valamihez ragaszkod\u00f3 (pl. He&#039;s _______ to his old ways.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ refusal = makacs visszautas\u00edt\u00e1s (pl. Her _______ refusal to cooperate was frustrating.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ attitude = makacs hozz\u00e1\u00e1ll\u00e1s (pl. The _______ attitude of the management made progress difficult.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>stubborn<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>stubborn<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>stubbornly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>stubbornness<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: stubborn mule \/ stubborn fact \/ stubborn stain \/ stubborn resistance<\/span><\/p><p>similar: obstinate \/ unyielding \/ inflexible \/ headstrong<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: flexible \/ compliant \/ amenable<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T11:32:03+00:00"},{"id":51311,"front":"<p>The manager decided to _______ the employee for repeated lateness. <em>(elbocs\u00e1t \/ kir\u00fag)<\/em><\/p><p>Let&#039;s _______ these minor concerns for now and focus on the main issue. <em>(elvet \/ mell\u0151z)<\/em><\/p><p>The judge will _______ the case if there isn&#039;t enough evidence. <em>(elutas\u00edt \/ ejt)<\/em><\/p><p>She tried to _______ his fears with a comforting smile, but he remained anxious. <em>(elhesseget \/ el\u0171z)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elbocs\u00e1t \/ elvet \/ elutas\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): felvesz \/ elfogad \/ megfontol<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a case = \u00fcgyet elutas\u00edt\/ejt (pl. The court decided to _______ the case due to lack of evidence.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an idea\/suggestion = \u00f6tletet\/javaslatot elvet (pl. They chose to _______ the idea of expanding abroad for now.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an employee = alkalmazottat elbocs\u00e1t (pl. The company had to _______ several employees during the recession.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a complaint = panaszt elutas\u00edt (pl. The customer service department decided to _______ her complaint.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a thought\/fear = gondolatot\/f\u00e9lelmet elhesseget (pl. He tried to _______ the negative thoughts from his mind.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>dismiss<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>dismissive<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>dismissively<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>dismissal<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>dismiss<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: dismiss a claim \/ dismiss an appeal \/ dismiss an argument \/ dismiss out of hand<\/span><\/p><p>similar: reject \/ disregard \/ fire \/ release<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: accept \/ consider \/ employ<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"dismiss\ndismissive\ndismissively","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-21T11:32:12+00:00"},{"id":51330,"front":"<p>It was a truly _______ gesture for him to offer his last piece of bread to the stranger. <em>(nagylelk\u0171 \/ nemes)<\/em><\/p><p>The _______ prize is awarded annually to individuals who have made outstanding contributions to humanity. <em>(nemes \/ kiemelked\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p>Despite his humble beginnings, he possessed a _______ spirit and an unwavering commitment to justice. <em>(nemes \/ erk\u00f6lcs\u00f6s)<\/em><\/p><p>The family could trace their lineage back to a long line of _______ knights and lords. <em>(nemesi \/ arisztokrata)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">nemes \/ nagylelk\u0171 \/ nemesi<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): aljas \/ k\u00f6z\u00f6ns\u00e9ges \/ hitv\u00e1ny<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ cause = nemes \u00fcgy (pl. He dedicated his life to a _______ cause.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ gesture = nagylelk\u0171 gesztus (pl. It was a _______ gesture to forgive his enemy.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ family = nemesi csal\u00e1d (pl. She came from an old _______ family.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ spirit = nemes l\u00e9lek (pl. He had a _______ spirit, always striving for good.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>noble<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>noble<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>nobly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>nobility<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: noble cause \/ noble gesture \/ noble family \/ noble spirit<\/span><\/p><p>similar: honorable \/ generous \/ dignified \/ aristocratic<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: dishonorable \/ ignoble \/ base<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"noble","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T16:36:27+00:00"},{"id":51263,"front":"<p>We need to _______ the damage caused by the storm before we can start repairs. <em>(felm\u00e9rni \/ meg\u00edt\u00e9lni)<\/em><\/p><p>The teacher will _______ the students&#039; progress based on their final exams and coursework. <em>(\u00e9rt\u00e9kelni \/ min\u0151s\u00edteni)<\/em><\/p><p>Researchers aim to _______ the effectiveness of the new drug through rigorous clinical trials. <em>(felm\u00e9rni \/ meg\u00e1llap\u00edtani)<\/em><\/p><p>She tried to _______ his motives, but his actions remained ambiguous. <