/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>pedestrian<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: pedestrian crossing \/ pedestrian zone \/ pedestrian safety \/ pedestrian traffic<\/span><\/p><p>similar: walker \/ foot traveler \/ on-foot \/ non-motorized<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: vehicle \/ motorist \/ driver<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":2,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"3 nap","good":"4 nap","easy":"5 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-01T10:57:38+00:00"},{"id":51318,"front":"<p>The old, abandoned house was known for its _______ occurrences, with strange lights and whispers reported by many. <em>(k\u00eds\u00e9rteties \/ szellemszer\u0171)<\/em><\/p><p>Scientists used _______ analysis to identify the chemical composition of the distant star, examining the different wavelengths of light it emitted. <em>(spektr\u00e1lis \/ sz\u00ednk\u00e9pelemz\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p>After the tragic event, a _______ silence fell over the crowd, a chilling quiet that spoke volumes. <em>(k\u00eds\u00e9rteties \/ borzongat\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p>Her performance had a _______ quality, as if she were a ghost dancing on stage, captivating the audience with her ethereal movements. <em>(szellemszer\u0171 \/ \u00e9terikus)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">k\u00eds\u00e9rteties \/ szellemszer\u0171 \/ spektr\u00e1lis<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): val\u00f3s\u00e1gos \/ k\u00e9zzelfoghat\u00f3 \/ anyagi<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ analysis = spektr\u00e1lis anal\u00edzis (pl. The lab conducted _______ analysis to identify the unknown substance.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ presence = k\u00eds\u00e9rteties jelenl\u00e9t (pl. Many reported a _______ presence in the old mansion.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ light = spektr\u00e1lis f\u00e9ny \/ k\u00eds\u00e9rteties f\u00e9ny (pl. The aurora borealis displayed a dazzling array of _______ light.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ silence = k\u00eds\u00e9rteties csend (pl. A _______ silence fell over the empty stadium.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>spectral<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>spectral<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>spectrally<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>spectrum<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: spectral analysis \/ spectral presence \/ spectral light \/ spectral image<\/span><\/p><p>similar: ghostly \/ phantom \/ eerie \/ supernatural<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: real \/ tangible \/ corporeal<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"spectral\nspectrally","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-18T18:25:44+00:00"},{"id":51320,"front":"<p>After years of practice, she became incredibly _______ in playing the piano, effortlessly performing complex pieces. <em>(\u00fcgyes \/ j\u00e1rtas)<\/em><\/p><p>To be truly _______ in a foreign language, one must not only understand grammar but also grasp cultural nuances. <em>(foly\u00e9kony \/ magabiztos)<\/em><\/p><p>The new software engineer is highly _______ in Python and C++, making him a valuable asset to the development team. <em>(szak\u00e9rt\u0151 \/ kompetens)<\/em><\/p><p>Her _______ command of legal terminology impressed the judges during the trial. <em>(mesteri \/ kiv\u00e1l\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">j\u00e1rtas \/ \u00fcgyes \/ szak\u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00fcgyetlen \/ tudatlan \/ hozz\u00e1 nem \u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in something = j\u00e1rtas valamiben (pl. He is proficient in several programming languages.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 highly _______ = nagyon j\u00e1rtas (pl. She is highly proficient at public speaking.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 become _______ = j\u00e1rtass\u00e1 v\u00e1lik (pl. With practice, you will become proficient.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ user = j\u00e1rtas felhaszn\u00e1l\u00f3 (pl. The software is designed for proficient users.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>proficiently<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>proficiency<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: proficient in \/ highly proficient \/ become proficient \/ proficient user<\/span><\/p><p>similar: skilled \/ competent \/ expert \/ adept<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: unskilled \/ incompetent \/ inexperienced<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"proficient\nproficiently\nproficiency","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T16:18:26+00:00"},{"id":51276,"front":"<p>The police managed to _______ the drug shipment before it reached the city. <em>(megakad\u00e1lyoz \/ lefoglal)<\/em><\/p><p>In tennis, a player can _______ their opponent&#039;s serve if they are fast enough. <em>(vissza\u00fct \/ elkap)<\/em><\/p><p>The intelligence agency was able to _______ the communication between the two hostile nations. <em>(lehallgat \/ elfog)<\/em><\/p><p>The knight bravely rode to _______ the princess from the dragon&#039;s lair. <em>(megment \/ kiszabad\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elfog \/ megakad\u00e1lyoz \/ lefoglal \/ megment \/ visszafog<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elenged \/ \u00e1tenged \/ seg\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a message = \u00fczenetet elfog\/lehallgat (pl. They managed to intercept a coded message.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a pass = passzt elfog\/elkap (pl. The defender intercepted the pass and scored.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a shipment = sz\u00e1ll\u00edtm\u00e1nyt elfog\/lefoglal (pl. Customs officials will intercept illegal goods.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ communication = kommunik\u00e1ci\u00f3t lehallgat\/elfog (pl. The spy agency can intercept enemy communications.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>intercept<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>interception<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>intercept<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: intercept a pass \/ intercept a message \/ intercept a shipment \/ intercept communication<\/span><\/p><p>similar: catch \/ stop \/ seize \/ block<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: release \/ allow \/ forward<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"intercept\ninterception","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"6 nap","easy":"7 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-19T17:03:50+00:00"},{"id":51312,"front":"<p>Starting a new business is a risky _______, but it can be very rewarding. <em>(v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ \u00fczleti kezdem\u00e9nyez\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>The government launched a new _______ to tackle unemployment in rural areas. <em>(projekt \/ kezdem\u00e9nyez\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>Her latest novel is an ambitious literary _______, blending historical fact with fantasy. <em>(v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ irodalmi k\u00eds\u00e9rlet)<\/em><\/p><p>The spirit of free _______ is crucial for economic growth and innovation. <em>(v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ gazdas\u00e1gi tev\u00e9kenys\u00e9g)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ kezdem\u00e9nyez\u00e9s \/ v\u00e1llalat<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): passzivit\u00e1s \/ tehetetlens\u00e9g \/ kudarcos pr\u00f3b\u00e1lkoz\u00e1s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 free _______ = szabad v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s (pl. The principles of free _______ are fundamental to capitalism.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 private _______ = mag\u00e1nv\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s (pl. The country encourages private _______ and foreign investment.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a joint _______ = k\u00f6z\u00f6s v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s (pl. They formed a joint _______ to develop the new software.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 spirit of _______ = v\u00e1llalkoz\u00f3 szellem (pl. The city has a strong spirit of _______ and innovation.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>enterprise<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>enterprising<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>enterprise<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: business enterprise \/ commercial enterprise \/ public enterprise \/ new enterprise<\/span><\/p><p>similar: venture \/ undertaking \/ project \/ company<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: inactivity \/ stagnation \/ passivity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"enterprise","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-22T16:23:00+00:00"},{"id":51295,"front":"<p>The tall grass began to _______ gently in the evening breeze. <em>(ringat\u00f3zik \/ lengedezik)<\/em><\/p><p>Despite the strong arguments, he refused to _______ from his original position. <em>(elt\u00e9r \/ enged)<\/em><\/p><p>The politician&#039;s charismatic speech was designed to _______ public opinion. <em>(befoly\u00e1sol \/ ir\u00e1ny\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>The ship began to _______ dangerously in the rough seas, making many passengers seasick. <em>(ingadozik \/ d\u00fcl\u00f6ng\u00e9l)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">ingat \/ befoly\u00e1sol \/ ringat\u00f3zik<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): stabiliz\u00e1l \/ megszil\u00e1rd\u00edt \/ ellen\u00e1ll<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ public opinion = befoly\u00e1solja a k\u00f6zv\u00e9lem\u00e9nyt (pl. His powerful speech began to _______ public opinion in his favor.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ back and forth = ide-oda ringat\u00f3zik (pl. The hammock began to _______ back and forth in the gentle wind.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 under the _______ of = valaki\/valami befoly\u00e1sa alatt (pl. The decision was made under the strong _______ of the CEO.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ with the music = ringat\u00f3zik a zene \u00fctem\u00e9re (pl. She began to _______ with the music, lost in the rhythm.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>sway<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>sway<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>sway<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: sway public opinion \/ sway back and forth \/ hold sway \/ sway from<\/span><\/p><p>similar: influence \/ oscillate \/ waver \/ dominate<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: stabilize \/ remain firm \/ resist<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-22T16:17:31+00:00"},{"id":51333,"front":"<p>The feeling of impending doom was _______ as the storm approached. <em>(elker\u00fclhetetlen \/ kiker\u00fclhetetlen)<\/em><\/p><p>For many, the need to earn a living is an _______ reality. <em>(megker\u00fclhetetlen \/ kiker\u00fclhetetlen)<\/em><\/p><p>The consequences of climate change are becoming increasingly _______. <em>(elker\u00fclhetetlen \/ megker\u00fclhetetlen)<\/em><\/p><p>He felt an _______ urge to confess his secret. <em>(ellen\u00e1llhatatlan \/ k\u00e9nyszer\u00edt\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elker\u00fclhetetlen \/ kiker\u00fclhetetlen \/ megker\u00fclhetetlen<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elker\u00fclhet\u0151 \/ kiker\u00fclhet\u0151 \/ megker\u00fclhet\u0151<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 an _______ truth = elker\u00fclhetetlen igazs\u00e1g (pl. The fact that we all age is an inescapable truth.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 an _______ conclusion = elker\u00fclhetetlen k\u00f6vetkeztet\u00e9s (pl. Given the evidence, the jury reached an inescapable conclusion.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ fate = elker\u00fclhetetlen sors (pl. He accepted his inescapable fate with dignity.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 an _______ fact = elker\u00fclhetetlen t\u00e9ny (pl. Death is an inescapable fact of life.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>inescapable<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>inescapable<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>inescapably<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: inescapable reality \/ inescapable truth \/ inescapable conclusion \/ inescapable fact<\/span><\/p><p>similar: unavoidable \/ inevitable \/ unpreventable \/ certain<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: avoidable \/ preventable \/ escapable<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-20T08:22:24+00:00"},{"id":51324,"front":"<p>After the divorce, the parents fought bitterly over the legal _______ of their children. <em>(gyermekfel\u00fcgyelet \/ fel\u00fcgyeleti jog)<\/em><\/p><p>The suspect was taken into police _______ for questioning regarding the robbery. <em>(\u0151rizet \/ letart\u00f3ztat\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>The ancient manuscript is kept under strict _______ in the museum&#039;s secure archives. <em>(\u0151rz\u00e9s \/ fel\u00fcgyelet)<\/em><\/p><p>The judge awarded sole _______ of the estate to the eldest son. <em>(gondnoks\u00e1g \/ vagyonkezel\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">\u0151rizet \/ fel\u00fcgyelet \/ gondnoks\u00e1g<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): szabads\u00e1g \/ elenged\u00e9s \/ f\u00fcggetlens\u00e9g<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 in _______ = \u0151rizetben (pl. He was taken in _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 legal _______ = jogi fel\u00fcgyelet (pl. The court granted legal _______ of the child to the mother.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 sole _______ = kiz\u00e1r\u00f3lagos fel\u00fcgyelet\/gondnoks\u00e1g (pl. She was awarded sole _______ of the children.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 take into _______ = \u0151rizetbe vesz (pl. The police took the suspect into _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 award _______ = fel\u00fcgyeletet\/gondnoks\u00e1got \u00edt\u00e9l (pl. The judge will award _______ next week.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>custody<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>custody<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: child custody \/ police custody \/ legal custody \/ sole custody<\/span><\/p><p>similar: guardianship \/ detention \/ care \/ supervision<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: freedom \/ release \/ liberty<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"custody","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-22T04:23:41+00:00"},{"id":51272,"front":"<p>Due to unforeseen _______, the wedding had to be postponed. <em>(k\u00f6r\u00fclm\u00e9nyek \/ helyzet)<\/em><\/p><p>The judge considered all the _______ before making a decision. <em>(t\u00e9nyez\u0151k \/ viszonyok)<\/em><\/p><p>The research paper analyzed the socio-economic _______ that contributed to the decline. <em>(h\u00e1tt\u00e9r \/ k\u00f6rnyezet)<\/em><\/p><p>She found herself in a difficult _______, with no easy way out. <em>(helyzet \/ \u00e1llapot)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">k\u00f6r\u00fclm\u00e9ny \/ helyzet \/ t\u00e9nyez\u0151 \/ viszony \/ \u00e1llapot<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): szabads\u00e1g \/ f\u00fcggetlens\u00e9g \/ egyszer\u0171s\u00e9g<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 under the _______ of = valaminek a _______ alatt (pl. under the _______ of his parents)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 given the _______ = a _______eket figyelembe v\u00e9ve (pl. given the _______, we should proceed cautiously)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 extenuating _______ = enyh\u00edt\u0151 _______ek (pl. there were extenuating _______ for his absence)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 adverse _______ = kedvez\u0151tlen _______ek (pl. the project faced adverse _______)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 difficult _______ = neh\u00e9z _______ek (pl. she overcame many difficult _______)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>circumstance<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>circumstance<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: difficult circumstances \/ unforeseen circumstances \/ extenuating circumstances \/ given the circumstances<\/span><\/p><p>similar: situation \/ condition \/ factor \/ state of affairs<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: certainty \/ freedom \/ simplicity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"circumstance","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":1,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-23T16:20:49+00:00"},{"id":51313,"front":"<p>The teacher will _______ the students on how to use the new software. <em>(oktat \/ tan\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>It is important to _______ your employees clearly about their responsibilities. <em>(utas\u00edt \/ eligaz\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>The manual will _______ you on the proper assembly of the furniture. <em>(\u00fatmutat\u00e1st ad \/ t\u00e1j\u00e9koztat)<\/em><\/p><p>Before you begin, I must _______ you to proceed with caution. <em>(utas\u00edt\u00e1st ad \/ felsz\u00f3l\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">utas\u00edt \/ oktat \/ tan\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): f\u00e9lrevezet \/ elt\u00e9veszt \/ nem tan\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ someone to do something = utas\u00edtani valakit valamire (pl. The manager will _______ the team to complete the report by Friday.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ in a subject = oktatni egy t\u00e1rgyban (pl. She was hired to _______ students in advanced mathematics.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ on safety procedures = oktatni biztons\u00e1gi elj\u00e1r\u00e1sokr\u00f3l (pl. All new employees are _______ed on safety procedures.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a lawyer = \u00fcgyv\u00e9det megb\u00edzni\/utas\u00edtani (pl. He decided to _______ a lawyer to handle his case.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>instruct<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>instructive<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>instructively<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>instruction<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>instruct<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: instruct someone \/ instruct on \/ instruct to \/ instruct a lawyer<\/span><\/p><p>similar: teach \/ educate \/ train \/ direct \/ command<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: mislead \/ misguide \/ confuse<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 nap","good":"2 nap","easy":"3 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-21T11:33:03+00:00"},{"id":51298,"front":"<p>When she heard the news, she called her mother _______ to share it. <em>(azonnal \/ r\u00f6gt\u00f6n)<\/em><\/p><p>The manager expects the report to be submitted _______ after the meeting concludes. <em>(halad\u00e9ktalanul \/ azonnal)<\/em><\/p><p>Upon receiving the distress signal, the rescue team set off _______. <em>(azonnal \/ r\u00f6gt\u00f6n)<\/em><\/p><p>He knew _______ that he had made a mistake, even before anyone else reacted. <em>(azonnal \/ r\u00f6gt\u00f6n)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">azonnal \/ r\u00f6gt\u00f6n \/ halad\u00e9ktalanul<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): k\u00e9s\u0151bb \/ lassan \/ id\u0151vel<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 do something _______ = azonnal megtenni valamit (pl. He decided to do it _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 go _______ = azonnal menni (pl. We need to go _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 know _______ = azonnal tudni (pl. She knew _______ that something was wrong.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 start _______ = azonnal elkezdeni (pl. Let&#039;s start _______ with the presentation.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>straightaway<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>straightaway<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: do it straightaway \/ go straightaway \/ know straightaway \/ start straightaway<\/span><\/p><p>similar: immediately \/ at once \/ instantly \/ promptly<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: later \/ eventually \/ presently<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-18T18:27:07+00:00"}]},"url":"\/flashcards\/38\/study","version":"2fc7632a2b863868c9df5c4c050ebabd","sharedProps":["errors","name","auth","sidebarOpen","flash"]}</script><div id="app"></div>